-- ProfileHandle — a social-media handle attached to a profile. Carries
-- both `profileId: EntityRef<"profile">` and `platform: EntityRef<"platform">`
-- — TWO EntityRef fields with DIFFERENT phantom names (not the same
-- phantom like profile_relationship's profileAId / profileBId). The
-- `handle` field refines String over the `format:handle` named-set
-- predicate (extracted as the `Handle` named atom for the same path-(b)
-- reason as profile_tag's Importance — `|`-refinement is type-decl-
-- level only).
--
-- Static rows: none. Identity (label / description / icon) is
-- registered by defineSystemEntity on the TS side.
--
-- Phase 3c of the system-entities sweep — see
-- workstreams/ts-elimination/briefs/phase-3c-profile-relations.md.
-- This is the largest entity in the Phase 3c batch (7 fields) and
-- exercises the broadest mix of shapes: bare EntityRef, named-refined
-- atom (Handle), bare Boolean (suspected), three Maybe Date fields.
-- Only `profileId` carries an override (→ "Profile") — the other six
-- field labels humanize cleanly ("Platform", "Handle", "Suspected",
-- "Valid From", "Valid To", "Verified At"). The brief's Watch-out §5
-- flags the `platform` field as `EntityRef<"platform">` (typed reference
-- to a platform entity row), NOT a String — don't flatten the type
-- because the field name suggests "platform code".

@entity
@label "Handle"
@description "String constrained to a valid handle (format:handle)"
Handle = String | value ∈ format:handle

@entity
@codeName "profile_handle"
@label "Profile Handle"
@description "A social-media handle attached to a profile"
@icon "at-sign"
@fieldLabel "profileId" "Profile"
ProfileHandle = ProfileHandle profileId: EntityRef<"profile"> platform: EntityRef<"platform"> handle: Handle suspected: Boolean validFrom: Maybe Date validTo: Maybe Date verifiedAt: Maybe Date
